      "content": "it's not just depression though. it's just math. i look at what we owe, the hours i work that barely cover it, and then i look at the kids needing things i can't give them. if i were gone, the insurance would kick in, the debt wouldn't be my responsibility anymore, and they could finally move forward without worrying about me failing them every single day. it's the only way the numbers actually make sense.",
